# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values below.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Backend API (server-only)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  The real Go backend origin. Consumed by next.config.ts's rewrites() to
#  proxy /api/* same-origin, so the admin session cookie is first-party to
#  this app regardless of which domain hosts the backend. NOT prefixed with
#  NEXT_PUBLIC_ — never sent to the browser.
BACKEND_API_URL=http://localhost:8080

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Razorpay Standard Checkout (public key only)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  The Razorpay Key ID used to open the Checkout modal client-side. This is
#  a publishable identifier, not a secret — it's safe to embed in the client
#  bundle, which is what the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix does. The matching secret
#  key lives only in the backend's RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET and must never appear
#  here. Use a TEST MODE key (rzp_test_...) for local development.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
